-- title:
--   Unramified fibre count equals the degree over ℂ(f)
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure which is a curve over $\mathbb{C}$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` — every nonzero element of $F$ has a principal divisor of degree zero, every place of $F$ has residue field finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ is free of rank one over $F$ — and which is of essentially finite type over $\mathbb{C}$. Here a place of $F$ over $\mathbb{C}$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, different from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring; for such a place $v$, $\mathrm{ord}_v$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, $v$ is called rational when $\mathbb{C}$ surjects onto its residue field, and $v.\mathrm{evalAt}(g)$ is the element of $\mathbb{C}$ mapping to the residue of $g$ when $g$ lies in the valuation subring (and $0$ otherwise). Let $f \in F$ be transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $E = \mathbb{C}(f)$ generated by $f$. Assume every place of $F$ and every place of $E$ is rational. Let $t \in \mathbb{C}$, and suppose there is a place $w_0$ of $F$ with $f$ in its valuation subring and $w_0.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = t$, and that every place $w$ of $F$ with $f$ in its valuation subring and $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = t$ satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_w(f - t) = 1$. Then the number of places $P$ of $F$ with $f \in P$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = t$ equals $[F : E]$. Since the cardinality is taken as `Nat.card`, which is $0$ on infinite types, the assertion includes the finiteness of this fibre.
--
--   This is the fundamental identity $\sum_w e_w f_w = n$ for the extension $F/\mathbb{C}(f)$, specialised to an attained value $t$ at which all ramification indices are one and, the constant field being algebraically closed, all residue degrees are one, so that the fibre of $\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ over $t$ has exactly $[F:\mathbb{C}(f)]$ elements. It supplies the fibre-size law used by [`AlgebraicCurve.isCoveringMapOn_evalAt`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.isCoveringMapOn_evalAt), and the proof cites the fundamental identity [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.sum_ramificationIndex_eq_finrank`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.sum_ramificationIndex_eq_finrank) together with the compatibility of evaluation with restriction of places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_card_fiber_eq_finrank_adjoin_of_ord_eq_one.lean

